    - Refactor the `BlogApp` class to ensure methods are single-responsibility focused. For instance, separating save/load logic into dedicated classes or methods would enhance clarity and maintainability.

In summary, the project framework is effective for a small-scale application, but improvements in security, data management, and user experience are crucial for enhancing the overall functionality and maintainability of the project. Implementing the suggestions will lead to a more robust application architecture.
